			}]
			x: 0.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["364B6665BE417076"]
			description: [
				"There is 5 tiers of Villagers:"
				"- &ePeasants&r"
				"- &aWorkers&r"
				"- &5Artisans&r"
				"- &cScholars&r"
				"- &bExcellence&r"
				""
				"Tier 2 Villagers can only be hired using Tier 1 Villagers &bSeals of Approval&r,"
				"Tier 3 Villagers using Tier 2  Seals of Approval, and so on."
				"Seals of Approval can be bought from level 5 Villagers."
				""
				"&6Tier 4 Villagers are picky and will require the most advanced and extravagant meals. There is only 1 Villager from Tier 5. Getting this Villager to max level will complete half of the end objective.&r"
			]
			icon: "trading_floor:trading_depot"
			id: "14EFC5F3A0624121"
			subtitle: "Villagers get very picky."
			tasks: [{
				id: "20E03CA7C8BFE58B"
				title: "Villager Tiers"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: -2.5d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["18F82432598BFED0"]
			description: [
				"From levels 1 to 4, villagers pay for food with cogs, which is the currency of The Company."
				"In &6Create: Hell's Kitchen&r, everything is set in so that you can power through the early, annoying stages of the early game if you know what to spend your cogs on."
				"&aEggMart&r will remain your most essential place to get crops throughout the game,"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"but will come in handy if you lack any type of material at some point in the game."
				"Make sure to spend wisely!"
				""
				"&aYou can access Eggmart at any moment by clicking the Dollar-Egg next to the Quest Book in the inventory screen menu. You can also access it with a keybind."
				""
				"&8Note: Eggmart is powered by the mod SDM Shop from Sixik."
			]
			icon: "numismatics:cog"
			id: "38F5BE5D2BDB9004"
			rewards: [{
				id: "3CF53E2031881F06"
				item: "numismatics:bank_terminal"
